From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Use in-process GPU for Crystal of Atlan

Crystal of Atlan's Seria executable embeds its CEF-based launcher UI, which
can hit Wine-Wayland GPU-process issues. Run its GPU process in-process while
keeping the workaround scoped to the game's installation path.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/process.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
index aaaaaaaaaaa..bbbbbbbbbbb 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -618,6 +618,7 @@ static const WCHAR *hack_append_command_line( const WCHAR *cmd )
         {L"Battle.net Launcher.exe", L" --in-process-gpu"},
         {L"Warframe\\Tools\\Launcher.exe", L" --in-process-gpu"},
         {L"Paradox Launcher.exe", L" --use-angle=gl"},
         {L"Montaro\\nw.exe", L" --use-gl=swiftshader"},
+        {L"Crystal of Atlan\\Seria\\Binaries\\Win64\\Seria.exe", L" --in-process-gpu"},
         {L"Aisling and the Tavern of Elves\\nw.exe", L" --use-gl=swiftshader"},
         {L"Snares of Ruin 2\\SoR2.exe", L" --use-gl=swiftshader"},
-- 
2.54.0
